:: 19A Rule: Don’t Look Back [en] {"position":"2475,450","size":"100,100"}
{
<!-- PAGE 19A: ESCAPE PATH - ASKED ABOUT FRIEND
     Outcome when protagonist asked staff about escape
     High stress: monster appears, must follow Rule 4 (don't look back) -->
(set: $sanity to it - 12)
(set: $dialogs to (a: 
  "I was still dissecting the staff member's behavior in my mind when I decided to steal one last look at his retreating figure. My blood turned to ice. His uniform—the one that was supposed to be a safe, reliable blue—had bled into a sickeningly vivid crimson.",
  "Samuel, don't—",
  "Before I could finish my warning, a piercing scream ripped through the air, only to be cut short by a sudden, suffocating silence." ,
  "(Then, I heard it. From the darkness directly behind me came a sound that defied logic: a woman’s desperate weeping, layered with the erratic, metallic crackle of an electrical short circuit.)",
  "(I couldn't move. I didn't want to know what was back there. Was my mind finally snapping? Was it a hallucination, or was it Her... that nightmare in the shape of a mascot?)",
  "At this moment, you should:"
))

(set: $names to (a: "", "Me", "", "", "", ""))
(set: $step to 1)
(set: $msgName to $names's ($step))
(set: $nextPassage to "none")

(display: "DialogBox")
(display: "Styles")
}

|choices)[
(button:)[[Do not look back, run for your life immediately]]
]

<!--According to Rule 4: Do not turn around. Do not acknowledge it.-->


:: 19B The Crimson Reveal [en] {"position":"2475,575","size":"100,100"}
{
(set: $sanity to it - 10)
(set: $dialogs to (a: 
  "I froze as I realized the staff member’s uniform had bled from a safe blue into a glaring, hostile scarlet.",
  "Samuel lost it. A sharp, jagged scream escaped his throat before I could cover his mouth. It was the one sound we couldn't afford to make.",
  "The sound acted like a beacon. The giant mascot, Mabel, snapped her head toward us. The moment her dead, glass eyes locked onto our horrified faces, she began to charge. Her movements were a sickening mix of mechanical stutters and predatory speed.",
  "There was no time for a plan. There was only the primal urge to survive.",
  "Where will you go?"
))

(set: $names to (a: "", "", "", "", ""))
(set: $step to 1)
(set: $msgName to $names's ($step))
(set: $nextPassage to "none")

(display: "DialogBox")
(display: "Styles")
}

|choices)[
(button:)[[Exit via the Staff Passage]]
(button:)[[Hide in a room within the Staff Passage]]
]


:: 22A The VIP’s Secret Tunnel [en] {"position":"2900,525","size":"100,100"}
{
(set: $dialogs to (a: 
  "What does that even mean?" ,
  "I asked, my voice trembling with rising anger.",
  "If they hate the system, why take it out on us? Why drag innocent people into this nightmare?",
  "My heart sank as the silence stretched.",
  "Are you saying... there’s no way out?",
  "Astor stared at the SCP badge in his hand, his brow furrowed.",
  "Not necessarily.",
  "...",
  "I have a friend—a VIP regular. We spent a lot of time here before... before all this. He once mentioned a hidden service tunnel inside 'Colorful World' that leads directly beyond the park perimeter.",
  "He looked up, his eyes flashing with a renewed sense of purpose.",
  "It’s our only shot. Let’s move."
))

(set: $names to (a: "Me", "", "Me", "", "Me", "", "Astor", "Astor", "Astor", "", "Astor"))
(set: $step to 1)
(set: $msgName to $names's ($step))
(set: $nextPassage to "The Drifter’s Sacrifice")

(display: "DialogBox")
(display: "Styles")
}


:: 22B The Only Shot [en] {"position":"2900,650","size":"100,100"}
{
(set: $dialogs to (a: 
  "Samuel’s eyes were bloodshot, his voice cracking as he yelled",
  "What does that even mean? If they hate the world, why take it out on us? Why drag innocent people into their nightmare?",
  "Astor stepped forward, his voice calm but heavy.",
  "I know it’s unfair, Samuel. But anger won't get us through the night.",
  "(I looked at them both, my heart sinking.)",
  "So... is that it? Are we trapped here forever?",
  "Astor paused, staring at the SCP badge in his hand as if searching for an answer. After a long silence, he looked up.",
  "Maybe not. I have a friend—a VIP regular. We spent a lot of time here before the 'change.' He once mentioned a service tunnel deep within 'Colorful World' that leads straight beyond the park perimeter.",
  "He tightened the straps on his bag, his eyes flashing with a renewed sense of purpose.",
  "Let’s move."
))

(set: $names to (a: "", "Samuel", "", "Astor", "", "Me", "", "Astor", "", "Astor"))
(set: $step to 1)
(set: $msgName to $names's ($step))
(set: $nextPassage to "DrifterStory")

(display: "DialogBox")
(display: "Styles")
}


:: Ask [en] {"position":"2225,450","size":"100,100"}
{
<!-- DIALOGUE CHOICE A: Ask the staff member for help
     This path reveals more about the park's danger
     Leads toward potential escape route discovery -->
(set: $dialogs to (a: 
  "I edged closer, my voice trembling.",
  "Hello? Please... do you know how we can leave this place?",
  "The man let out a dry, mocking chuckle. His eyes swept over us with pure scorn." ,
  "The park closes at ten-thirty sharp,",
  "Didn't you bother to read the signs? You're lucky I'm not on the enforcement squad. If I were, you wouldn't even be 'present' anymore.",
  "He laughed, a cold, hollow sound.",
  "The chances of getting out now are slim to none. Once you're stuck here, the park rarely lets go.",
  "His words plunged Samuel and me into a fresh wave of panic. Watching our faces drain of color, the staff member seemed to relish our fear.",
  "But,",
  "he continued with a glint of malicious glee in his eyes,",
  "I do know a place that might grant your little wish. Follow me.",
))

(set: $names to (a: "", "Me", "", "???", "???", "", "???", "", "???", "", "???"))
(set: $step to 1)
(set: $msgName to $names's ($step))
(set: $nextPassage to "The Erased Street")

(display: "DialogBox")
(display: "Styles")
}

<!-- CHOICE TRACKER: Asked about friend - Ending-1 impact -->


:: Astor’s Revelation [en] {"position":"2775,575","size":"100,100"}
{
<!-- PAGE 21: REVELATION
     Astor explains the true nature of the park
     SCP Foundation connection revealed
     Split based on whether Samuel was mentioned in earlier scenes -->(set: $sanity to it - 6)
(set: $dialogs to (a: 
  "Astor reached into his pocket and handed me a worn ID badge. The letters SCP were printed boldly across the top. ",
  "Do you know anything about the SCP Foundation?",
  "I've heard rumors, but..." ,
  "They're an organization that deals with things that shouldn't exist,",
  "We found some files back in the maze. These monsters... before they became this, they were people who hated the rules and constraints of society. They felt suffocated by them.",
  "He looked toward the door, where the mechanical weeping of Mabel still echoed.",
  "It seems that hatred didn't die with them. Their resentment has fermented into something dark, something hungry for revenge. Now, they use the very thing they hated—Rules—to trap and destroy us."
))

(set: $names to (a: "", "Astor", "Me", "Astor", "Astor", "", "Astor"))
(set: $step to 1)
(set: $msgName to $names's ($step))
(if: $isAskingAboutFriend) [(set: $nextPassage to "22A The VIP’s Secret Tunnel")]
(else:)[(set: $nextPassage to "22B The Only Shot")]
(display: "DialogBox")
(display: "Styles")
}


