:: The Erased Street [en] {"position":"2350,500","size":"100,100"}
{
<!-- PAGE 18: THE ILLUSION REVEALED
     Unnatural cleanup of massacre scene
     Staff member's true nature becomes clear
     Splits into 19A (asking about friend) or 19B (didn't ask) -->
(set: $dialogs to (a: 
  "He led us back to the main thoroughfare of the park. My breath hitched in my throat—what I saw was impossible. The street that had been a slaughterhouse moments ago, littered with bodies and soaked in crimson, was now unnaturally clean. It was as if the chaos had been erased from existence.",
  "What... what happened?",
  "Samuel stammered, his eyes bulging. He rubbed them vigorously, convinced he was hallucinating. " ,
  "I was just as paralyzed by shock. I knelt and touched the ground; it was dry, pristine, without a single trace of the carnage we had witnessed. I looked up at the staff member in the dark blue uniform.",
  "Is this it?",
  "I whispered.",
  "He offered an unfathomable smile, one that sent a chill down my spine.",
  "This is as much help as I can provide.",
  'To my surprise, Samuel actually muttered a "thank you" to him. Without a word of farewell, the man turned and strode away, merging back into the darkness.'
))

(set: $names to (a: "", "Samuel", "", "", "Me", "", "", "Staff", ""))
(set: $step to 1)
(set: $msgName to $names's ($step))
(if: $isAskingAboutFriend) [(set: $nextPassage to "19A Rule: Don’t Look Back")]
(else:)[(set: $nextPassage to "19B The Crimson Reveal")]
(display: "DialogBox")
(display: "Styles")
}


